    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Automated External Defibrillators (AEDs) are compact, portable, effective and low-maintenance devices that can be used by non-medical personnel with minimal training, in non-clinical settings in under-resourced communities, to promptly defibrillate patients with out of hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA). Many countries around the world have guidelines, legislation and federal grants that dictate the number and placement of AEDs in public places. In Pakistan, no such legislations exist. The question is, what's happening on the ground?",
